Locked decision set:
- D1 = E: external conventions.md + per-verse /clear. Decouples accumulated expertise from lost independence — learning moves to a reviewable conventions.md, so each session resets per verse and R1 regains s1-grade blind independence "for free". Kills last run's two failure modes (agy context-decay + /compact loss).
- D2 = Hybrid (Q2): blind R1 + blind R2 (s1 Trigger 1/2 machinery intact) -> escalate to sealed-bid R2.5 deliberation ONLY on Level-2/3 instability (the 3:11-class verses s1 can only flag). Original "largest code delta" mostly evaporates because per-verse reset restores blindness.
- D3 = Q3-D batched: no raw-answer feedback; a scribe extracts distilled conventions per-chapter, regression-gates each (reusing s1's run_prompt_regression), versions them.

Reconciliation with Joshua's live-obe CRUX: persistent processes (tabs stay alive & leashed) + per-verse-fresh contexts (/clear) + externalized learning (conventions.md). The panel is still 3 bound colleagues consulting a shared reviewed notebook.

Why this lets s10 rival/surpass s1: same independence as s1, PLUS (1) conventions pre-align format/convention noise so false-disagreements vanish and residual splits are 100% genuine ambiguity; (2) R2.5 actually resolves genuine ambiguity amnesia cannot; (3) cheaper as conventions settle. Residual risk: conventions.md = new single trust-point = s1's prompt in finer form, guarded by the same regression gate + per-line revertibility + empirical per-convention FHL-truth scoring.

